Description: antinomie: add the generated table of x86-64 system calls
 native_syscalls.h lists every native x86-64 system call of Linux 6.12.94
 (463 slots): whether the slot exists, its argument count, which
 arguments are pointers and which are strings, and each argument's name
 and C type, as the kernel declares them. It is generated from the
 pinned source and is not meant to be edited by hand.
 .
 The recorder in the next patch uses it to decide which calls it traces,
 how many arguments an event carries, and what to name a pointer
 argument it has no decoder for. It is a patch of its own so that the
 review of the recorder is not buried in data; nothing includes it yet,
 so this patch changes no object.
 .
 No kernel file outside kernel/antinomie is touched, and the contract
 does not change.
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-26

---
